    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50692" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vēsīcārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		vesica, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the
			bladder</i>, <i>bladder-.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aqua,</span>”
				i. e. <i>curing pain in the bladder</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Marc. Emp. 26</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp.
			146</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vēsīcārĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f. (herba), <i>a
				plant that cures pain in the bladder</i>, <i>bladder - wort</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 21, 31, 105, §
		177</span></i>.</div>
